# Raw data: never versioned. It is downloaded from the source cited in the README
# and saved under the exact filename the scripts expect.
# Naming convention (phase 2):  origen_tema_periodo_version.csv
#
# Replace the line below with the actual pattern for this case, e.g.:
#   datos/crudos/kaggle_tema_2020-2026_2026-01-15.csv
datos/crudos/*.csv

# Keep small reference sources that DO belong in the repo by un-ignoring them
# explicitly, one line each. Example:
#   !datos/crudos/bls_cpi-u_anual_1997-2026_2026-07-28.csv

# Derived datasets: regenerated by `python notebooks/procesar.py`.
#
# Note the trailing /* instead of /: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so `datos/limpios/` followed by `!datos/limpios/.gitkeep` would never re-admit the
# file and the folder would not reach a new repo at all. Ignoring the CONTENT keeps
# the exception reachable.
datos/limpios/*
!datos/limpios/.gitkeep
datos/intermedios/*
!datos/intermedios/.gitkeep

# OS / environment junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
